  "notes": "Controlled contract NEGATIVES (spec 3.1/3.2): every error step must be rejected pre-header with the pinned status + stable capability code + field path + reason, in the ENTRY's own error shape, with no success terminal, zero active permits and zero outbound upstream requests. The mock marker is present in every request only so the authorized/unauthorized degradation pair stays byte-identical; error steps never reach the wire (upstream_requests=0). The last step is the explicit authorization POSITIVE: the same request plus the grant header must succeed and really degrade. Cross-project tokens are minted with manifest.continuation_envelope.drive_key_utf8 and cross_project_id so the HMAC passes and the PROJECT BINDING branch is the one that fails. Corrupt/truncated SSE negatives are already covered by ConversionEngineIntegrationTest / ConversionServiceTest / MockUpstreamDeepSeekTest. File references (input_file / file_id) are denied by the ENGINE ownership guard BEFORE conversion: the drive answers 404 with the gateway-generic body (expected.resource_denial), while the entry codec's own 400 capability rejection stays pinned as expected.error and is asserted at codec level.",
